<h2>TWIA, flood insurance, and CRS in Portland</h2>
<p>San Patricio County is in the TWIA designated catastrophe area. Many Portland owners therefore have a homeowners policy that excludes wind and hail, a separate TWIA policy for wind and hail, and a flood policy. TWIA covers wind and hail only, and TWIA claims generally must be filed within one year of the date of loss. Our <a href="/services/twia-windstorm-claims/">TWIA windstorm claims</a> page walks through that process.</p>
<p>Flood is a separate question. Standard homeowners policies generally exclude flood, and flood coverage comes from the NFIP or a private flood policy. Based on FEMA Community Status Book data (April 2025), Portland participates in the NFIP but not the Community Rating System, so Portland policies do not get a CRS discount. NFIP coverage generally starts 30 days after purchase, so buy it well before a storm is in the Gulf.</p>
<p>Roof repairs and re-roofs in the catastrophe area fall under the TDI Windstorm Inspection Program, and properties built, altered, or repaired on or after January 1, 1988 need a windstorm certificate of compliance to be TWIA-eligible. Ask your roofer how windstorm inspection will be handled before the old roof comes off. For local permit requirements, contact the City of Portland directly.</p>

<h2>How we help Portland property owners</h2>
<p>We inspect the full property, not only the roof: siding, windows, screens, fences, gutters, HVAC units, and interior water damage. We prepare an itemized estimate, organize photos and documents, and communicate with your insurer or TWIA. If you already have an offer that seems low, an <a href="/services/insurance-estimate-review/">insurance estimate review</a> can show what may be missing, and our <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid claims</a> page explains common reasons for gaps.</p>
<p>Portland owners often ask whether hail that only "looks" cosmetic is worth reporting. Some policies limit or exclude cosmetic damage to metal roofing or siding, while functional damage such as fractured shingles or punctured panels is usually treated differently. Corpus Christi Public Adjuster reviews your actual policy language before advising on how to present a hail claim.</p>
<p>To check what has been reported near your address, try our <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup tool</a>. When you are ready, request a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a> or call or text [[phone]].</p>
